Someone in #nethack asked if there was a way to figure out all the
possible words NetHack can ask you about in inventory letters. For
example,

What do you want to eat? [bABY or ?*]

The full list is at the bottom of this posting. The Perl script I used
to generate the list follows. I use /x in the regex so I can break up
the long lines. It could be a bit shorter for sure (for example, use a
variable $v to keep (a?b?c?...y?z?) and use /^$v$v$/) but this is what
I came up with at time.

perl -nle 'print lc($1).uc($2) if
/^(a?b?c?d?e?f?g?h?i?j?k?l?m?n?o?p?q?r?s?t?u?v?x?y?z?)
(a?b?c?d?e?f?g?h?i?j?k?l?m?n?o?p?q?r?s?t?u?v?w?x?y?z?)$/ix'
/usr/share/dict/words

